      <!-- SECTION 4: Bank Yards vs. Loose Yards vs. Compacted Yards -->
      <section id="geotechnical" class="bg-white p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 shadow-2xs space-y-5 scroll-mt-20">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-100 pb-4">
          <span class="text-[11px] font-bold text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-50 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md uppercase tracking-wider">Geotechnical Earthwork</span>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 mt-2">Bank Yards vs. Loose Yards vs. Compacted Yards (Swell Mechanics)</h2>
        </div>

        <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
          In civil engineering and site grading, earth does not occupy constant volume throughout the construction lifecycle. Soil particles naturally settle over millennia into an in-situ matrix. Once excavated by a backhoe, voids and air pockets expand the volume. When rolled under a vibratory compactor, voids collapse. Earthwork contracts strictly differentiate three volumetric states:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-blue-700 block">BCY · Bank Cubic Yards</span>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 mt-1">In-Situ / Natural State</div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
              Material in its virgin, undisturbed natural ground condition prior to excavation or blasting. Earthwork cut surveys quantify volume in BCY.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-amber-700 block">LCY · Loose Cubic Yards</span>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 mt-1">Excavated / Truck Bed State</div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
              Material after excavation and disturbance. Entrained air causes soil particles to swell. <strong>Dump truck hauling capacities and disposal fees are calculated in LCY.</strong>
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-700 block">CCY · Compacted Cubic Yards</span>
            <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 mt-1">Mechanically Densified State</div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
              Material placed, moisture-conditioned, and compacted with heavy rollers or vibratory plates into structural fill. Fill placement contracts quantify volume in CCY.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 pt-2">The Swell & Shrinkage Equations</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
          To calculate how many dump trucks you need to haul away an excavation hole, multiply Bank Yards by the material's swell percentage:
        </p>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3.5 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
            <span class="text-amber-400 font-bold block mb-1">Hauling Equation (Swell):</span>
            LCY = BCY × (1 + Swell Percentage)
          </div>
          <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white p-3.5 rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold block mb-1">Fill Equation (Shrinkage):</span>
            CCY = LCY × (1 - Shrinkage Percentage)
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200 mt-3">
          <table class="w-full text-xs text-left">
            <thead class="bg-slate-100 text-slate-800 font-bold">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-3.5 py-2">Soil Classification</th>
                <th class="px-3 py-2 text-right">Swell % (In-Bank to Loose)</th>
                <th class="px-3 py-2 text-right">Shrinkage % (Loose to Compacted)</th>
                <th class="px-3.5 py-2">Typical Earthwork Application</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 text-slate-700">
              <tr>
                <td class="px-3.5 py-2 font-bold text-slate-900">Clean Washed Sand & Gravel</td>
